{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Seven days.</b> Consecutive." "<b>The priest shall put them on.</b> Who shall arise from among his sons in his stead, for the high priesthood — when they appoint him to be High Priest." "<b>Who shall come into the Tent of Meeting.</b> That priest who is designated to enter the innermost sanctum on the Day of Atonement — and this is the High Priest, for the service of the Day of Atonement is valid only through him." "<b>In his stead from among his sons.</b> This teaches that if a High Priest has a son to fill his place, they appoint him High Priest in his stead." "<b>The priest in his stead from among his sons.</b> From here is a proof that every occurrence of the word כֹּהֵן is an active participle, an actual serving priest — therefore the tevir cantillation is drawn before it."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:36.829270441Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}